---
/**
 * The click-to-play island: a script, and nothing else.
 *
 * It renders no markup on purpose. Every facade is already in the page, built
 * at compile time by `src/markdown/wikilinks.ts` as a poster inside a link to
 * the video, so this file has nothing to draw and nothing to fetch: it upgrades
 * a link that already works into a player the reader asked for.
 *
 * The component exists in order to be *conditionally imported*, exactly as
 * `HoverPreview.astro` does. A bare `<script>` in `Note.astro` behind
 * `{config.features.embeds && …}` would still ship: Astro hoists and bundles
 * component scripts at compile time regardless of the surrounding conditional.
 * Only dropping the import takes the script out of the module graph. See
 * `JOTTER_EMBEDS` in `astro.config.ts`.
 */
---

<script>
  import '../scripts/embed.js'
</script>
